        "role": "user"
      },
      {
        "content": "The main thing is this. If the case resolves as a buyback, the manufacturer takes the vehicle back and refunds what you paid toward it. Our fees and costs are paid by the manufacturer, so you never get a bill from us. If there's money recovered above the buyback, that's the only part split fifty-fifty. For the sake of argument, if the buyback is fifty thousand and the case settles for a hundred thousand, the first fifty is all yours, and the extra fifty gets split, so you'd get seventy-five thousand. The buyback can also include a mileage offset, but that's a fixed deduction under the law based on the miles before the problem first showed up. That's the whole thing in a nutshell. What questions can I answer before I walk you through signing?",
        "created_timestamp": 1792353867692,
        "message_id": "message_666a0b8c9d9352856c24f8d9",
